", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Will, May, Might", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is \u2018ll.<br/><br/> You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.<br/><br/>The modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb.<br/> <br/>They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen.<br/> <br/><span class=\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br/> <br/><span class=\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh Sally, you may just be one of the best freelance journalists I know! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I might start my new job on Thursday. I'll be really nervous.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Opinions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can express an opinion using one of the expressions below:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Some people say that ...</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">(That's) The/the general consensus \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">As far as I'm concerned, \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Personally, I think \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">In my opinion, \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Sounds like \u2026 </span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'd say that \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I believe that \u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">What I mean is \u2026</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What I mean is, you might become a managing editor one day, Sally!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sounds like you're going to work long hours!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "masthead ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a printed list in each edition of a magazine, with people's names ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is your name going to be put on the masthead?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about work with a friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time working ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to put in many hours. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to brag", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to talk proudly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to brag to everyone about your new job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a long way to go ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a lot of work to do ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a long way to go before I can become an editor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "managing editor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who supervises the day-to-day operations of a publication ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You might become the managing editor of the magazine in the future!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consensus", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an opinion that everyone in a group agrees with ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's the general consensus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Pretend your friend needs some advice. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose 2 different jobs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your friend wants to know which of the two jobs to choose in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue (10-12) between you and your friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your opinion about the jobs with them. Remember to introduce your opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your dialogue. Practice reading your dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I introduce my opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about different jobs with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about jobs and work. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can say what I'm doing in the future. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can introduce an o